237
00:17:21,900 --> 00:17:22,840
the way you smell.

238
00:17:25,300 --> 00:17:26,660
Hey, Ross, what are you doing?

239
00:17:27,220 --> 00:17:28,620
Hey, Joe, you want to open the window?

240
00:17:28,960 --> 00:17:30,080
Oh, yeah, we...

241
00:17:31,420 --> 00:17:32,620
What are you doing out there?

242
00:17:32,780 --> 00:17:34,140
I, I, um...

243
00:17:34,140 --> 00:17:35,560
Oh, my gosh, you must be freezing.

244
00:17:35,760 --> 00:17:36,380
You know what you need?

245
00:17:36,700 --> 00:17:39,020
How about a nice steaming cup of hot mocklet?

246
00:17:44,180 --> 00:17:45,380
Reg, come on, open up.

247
00:17:46,640 --> 00:17:48,000
Reg, come on, come on.

248
00:17:48,080 --> 00:17:49,600
You gotta give me another chance.

249
00:17:50,260 --> 00:17:50,620
No.

250
00:17:51,980 --> 00:17:52,260
No?

251
00:17:52,660 --> 00:17:53,600
That's what I said.

252
00:17:54,220 --> 00:17:55,280
Look, maybe we should go.

253
00:17:55,440 --> 00:17:56,880
No, you guys, you really don't have to go.

254
00:17:57,000 --> 00:17:57,680
We're done talking.

255
00:17:57,940 --> 00:17:59,540
Reg, come on, look, I know how you must feel.

256
00:17:59,540 --> 00:18:01,200
No, you don't, Ross.

257
00:18:03,100 --> 00:18:05,500
Imagine the worst things you think about yourself.

258
00:18:06,140 --> 00:18:08,100
Now, how would you feel if the one person

259
00:18:08,100 --> 00:18:10,280
that you trusted the most in the world

260
00:18:10,280 --> 00:18:12,020
not only thinks them, too,

261
00:18:12,460 --> 00:18:14,400
but actually uses them

262
00:18:14,400 --> 00:18:16,460
as reasons not to be with you?

263
00:18:16,700 --> 00:18:17,280
No, but, but...

264
00:18:17,980 --> 00:18:19,220
See, I want to be with you

265
00:18:19,220 --> 00:18:20,860
in spite of all those things.

266
00:18:21,940 --> 00:18:24,480
Oh, well, that's, that's mighty big of you, Ross.

267
00:18:24,700 --> 00:18:25,620
I said don't go!

268
00:18:29,260 --> 00:18:30,060
You know what?

269
00:18:30,900 --> 00:18:31,320
You know what?

270
00:18:31,400 --> 00:18:33,900
If, if things were the other way around,

271
00:18:34,260 --> 00:18:36,080
there is nothing you could put on the list

272
00:18:36,080 --> 00:18:38,680
that would, that would ever make me not want to be with you.

273
00:18:39,600 --> 00:18:42,060
Well, then I guess that's the difference between us.

274
00:18:42,960 --> 00:18:44,400
See, I'd never make a list.

275
00:19:00,840 --> 00:19:02,440
I never know how long you're supposed to wait

276
00:19:02,440 --> 00:19:03,620
in this type of situation

277
00:19:03,620 --> 00:19:04,940
before you can talk again, you know?

278
00:19:07,380 --> 00:19:08,420
Maybe a little longer.

279
00:19:14,220 --> 00:19:15,680
Now, in some of these recipes,

280
00:19:15,820 --> 00:19:17,480
the quantities may seem just a little unusual.

281
00:19:18,080 --> 00:19:20,780
Uh, like these coconut mocklet holiday nut bars.

282
00:19:21,020 --> 00:19:22,780
I've indicated four cups of coconut

283
00:19:22,780 --> 00:19:24,220
and four cups of crushed nut

284
00:19:24,220 --> 00:19:26,760
and only, uh, one tablespoon of mocklet.

285
00:19:28,640 --> 00:19:29,380
Doesn't matter.

286
00:19:30,040 --> 00:19:30,340
What?

287
00:19:31,300 --> 00:19:33,080
Our FDA approval didn't come through.

288
00:19:34,120 --> 00:19:36,020
Something about laboratory rats.

289
00:19:38,020 --> 00:19:39,380
Oh, gosh, I'm sorry.

290
00:19:40,000 --> 00:19:40,380
Yeah.

291
00:19:41,100 --> 00:19:42,420
Well, anywho, here's your check.

292
00:19:44,040 --> 00:19:45,460
Thank you for all the trouble you went through.

293
00:19:46,940 --> 00:19:48,460
Um, listen, you didn't, uh,

294
00:19:48,940 --> 00:19:50,660
eat a lot of it while you were cooking, did you?

295
00:19:51,360 --> 00:19:52,640
Well, I ate some.

296
00:19:52,880 --> 00:19:54,300
Oh, some. That's fine. Some is fine.

297
00:19:54,400 --> 00:19:55,160
Some is not a lot.

298
00:19:56,180 --> 00:19:56,560
Okay.

299
00:19:57,100 --> 00:19:59,780
So it doesn't burn when you pee, does it?

300
00:20:13,000 --> 00:20:13,480
Hello?

301
00:20:14,500 --> 00:20:14,940
Hi.

302
00:20:17,660 --> 00:20:18,700
Is that him again?

303
00:20:19,460 --> 00:20:20,680
Tell him I'd come to the phone,

304
00:20:20,780 --> 00:20:22,540
but my ankles are weighing me down.

305
00:20:25,640 --> 00:20:27,980
Listen, I-I don't think this is the best time.

306
00:20:28,360 --> 00:20:31,000
Look, can... can you do something for me?

307
00:20:31,260 --> 00:20:32,000
Sure, what?

308
00:20:34,080 --> 00:20:34,560
Okay.

309
00:20:35,580 --> 00:20:36,060
I'll be right back.

310
00:20:36,080 --> 00:20:37,120
All right.

311
00:20:41,000 --> 00:20:41,620
Music!

312
00:20:50,420 --> 00:20:53,880
The next one's dedicated to Rachel from Ross.

313
00:20:54,580 --> 00:20:57,580
Rachel, he wants you to know he's deeply sorry for what he did,

314
00:20:57,640 --> 00:21:00,580
and he hopes you can find it in your heart to forgive him.

315
00:21:01,000 --> 00:21:04,880
See the stone set in your eyes

316
00:21:04,880 --> 00:21:09,100
See the phone twist in your side

317
00:21:09,100 --> 00:21:14,120
I'll wait for you

318
00:21:18,200 --> 00:21:21,880
Sleight of hand and twist of faith

319
00:21:22,420 --> 00:21:26,920
On a bed of nails she makes me waste

320
00:21:26,920 --> 00:21:31,680
And I'll wait without you

321
00:21:31,680 --> 00:21:34,420
Uh, we've just gotten a call from Rachel

322
00:21:34,420 --> 00:21:36,500
and she told us what Ross did.

323
00:21:37,020 --> 00:21:38,440
It's pretty appalling.

324
00:21:38,740 --> 00:21:40,040
And, Ross, if you're listening,

325
00:21:40,540 --> 00:21:42,120
I don't want to play your song anymore.

326
00:21:48,640 --> 00:21:51,820
Why don't we devote our time to a couple that stands a chance?

327
00:21:52,100 --> 00:21:54,300
Avery, Michelle, sorry she hit you with her car,

328
00:21:54,400 --> 00:21:56,180
and she hopes you two will work it out.

329
00:21:57,720 --> 00:22:03,220
There's a room where I can go

330
00:22:03,220 --> 00:22:09,260
And tell my secrets too

331
00:22:09,260 --> 00:22:13,460
In my room

332
00:22:16,220 --> 00:22:19,220
In my room

333
00:22:20,220 --> 00:22:22,720
In my room

334
00:22:22,720 --> 00:22:26,220
In my room

335
00:22:27,220 --> 00:22:29,060
In my room

336
00:22:31,280 --> 00:22:33,320
Hi. Thanks for coming in again.

337
00:22:33,460 --> 00:22:35,800
Oh, not at all. I have no morals and I need the cash.

338
00:22:36,680 --> 00:22:37,620
It's like I'm looking in a mirror.

339
00:22:40,240 --> 00:22:42,640
Anyway, they're called pistachios.

340
00:22:43,600 --> 00:22:46,280
Now, they taste exactly like pistachios,

341
00:22:46,380 --> 00:22:48,840
but they're made primarily of reconstituted fish bits.

342
00:22:50,340 --> 00:22:51,520
Here, try one.

343
00:22:52,760 --> 00:22:53,460
All right.

344
00:22:53,720 --> 00:22:55,060
You're not allergic to anything, are you?

345
00:22:55,980 --> 00:22:56,660
Cat hair.

346
00:22:56,660 --> 00:22:57,800
Oh, sorry.
